    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440-a5">

                <pb facs="0411" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg337"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>

                <head>Mr. Bigelow to Mr. Delbetz</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 4, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I am sensibly affected by the very cordial
                    letter which you have pleased to address to me on the occasion of the horrible
                    crime which has struck down our President, Mr. Lincoln. Nothing, in my view of
                    it, can more contribute to strengthen the very cordial relations which unite our
                    two nations than the evidences of sympathy emanating from such men as you.
                    Please accept, sir, the assurance of my most distinguished and cordial
                    respect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN BIGELOW.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p rendition="#flush">M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Delbetz.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
